<title>USA: Federal-Mogul president-operations resigns.</title>
<headline>Federal-Mogul president-operations resigns.</headline>
<dateline>SOUTHFIELD, Mich. 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Federal-Mogul Corp said Friday Wayne Smith, one of two of the company's presidents-operations, resigned effective immediately to pursue other opportunities.</p>
<p>Smith managed the company's worldwide aftermarket operations.</p>
<p>Federal-Mogul's acting chief executive Robert Miller said Alan Johnson, the company's president-operations focusing on manufacturing operations, will temporarily cover Smith's responsibilities.  Permanent management decisions will be made when the new chief executive has been chosen, the company said.</p>
<p>--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787</p>
